===persian===

گوش‌هایم در حیرتِ دیدن...
چشم‌هایم در حسرتِ شنیدن...
ای عشق...
من آوازِ تو را نقاشی می‌کنم...
۱۳۶۹/۳/۲۹

===machine===

My ears in the wonder of seeing...
my eyes in the longing to hear...
O love...
I am painting your song...
1369/3/29

===lantern===

My ears astonished at seeing...
my eyes aching to hear...
O love —
I am painting your song...

1369/3/29

===translation===

===footnotes===

Jafari was a painter before he was anything else, and the last line is not only a figure:
painting a song is the literal description of his working life. The same crossing runs through
pages 129 and 130, where he sees with his ears.
